onents/report/views/index.tsx`\n    35→\n    36→**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n    37→\n    38→## Recommended Skills\n    39→\n    40→- **compact-ui-design**: Use `.claude/skills/compact-ui-design.md` for high-quality UI design references and patterns\n    41→\n    42→## Notes\n    43→\n    44→This requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n    45→\n    46→## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n    47→\n    48→1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n    49→   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n    50→   - title: 2-6 word summary\n    51→   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n    52→\n    53→2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n    54→   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n    55→   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n    56→\n    57→3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n    58→\n    59→Begin implementation now.\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8a4f9ca-6a40-4b19-853c-2be96846861c","uuid":"ea8c50b3-3531-46b5-a1c4-d04f41ae9c6a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\idea-656762d1-add-sticky-section-headers-in.md","content":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Add sticky section headers in long scrolling views\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: ui\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: manual\n- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:44:46 AM\n\n## Description\nEntitiesView and AnalysisView have collapsible sections that scroll off-screen. Add position:sticky top-0 z-10 to section headers with a subtle backdrop-blur-sm bg-white/80 (or theme equivalent). Headers stay visible as users scroll through long sections.\n\n## Reasoning\nUsers lose context when section headers scroll away in long lists. Sticky headers maintain orientation and provide constant access to section controls (collapse toggle). This is especially valuable for EntitiesView with multiple entity type sections.\n\n## Context\n\n**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n\n### Context: Report Views\n\n**Description**: Full-page report views for different sections: overview, findings, sources, analysis, entities, and perspectives. Each view provides deep-dive content for its domain.\n**Related Files**:\n- `src/components/report/views/OverviewView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/FindingsView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/SourcesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/AnalysisView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/EntitiesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/PerspectivesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/index.tsx`\n\n**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\n- **compact-ui-design**: Use `.claude/skills/compact-ui-design.md` for high-quality UI design references and patterns\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log you